  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Eswatini - Disaster Management and Resilience</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is a preparedness and livelihood project that aims to assist communities to better respond and recover from the impacts of the forecasted El Nino. The livelihood strategies planned for this project include communal gardens where livelihood groups will be identified and gathered through trainings on conservation agriculture and assisted to revive and/or establish their communal gardens used for crop production. With this intervention, the project will aim to increase their agricultural production. Communities through their disaster risk reduction committees will be trained so that they ultimately understand their vulnerabilities and capacities to understand how the intervention offered by BERCS will assist them in the long run&#xA0;This will ensure sustainability of the interventions even beyond the project lifecycle. The most food insecure communities will also be identified and assisted through cash-based transfers to cover their household needs. In enhancing disaster preparedness, the project will take a twist to develop a flood Early Action Protocol to ensure that BERCS has access to automatic funding to act early in anticipation to flood events.</narrative>
  </description>
